    "notes": "1. The 'total_revenue' field is mapped from the 'Total revenues and other income' line, which is the sum of its three listed components. Each component is listed individually in the array as per rule #4. 2. For 'total_operating_cost', all items listed under 'Costs and other deductions' are included, except for 'Interest expense' (which is mapped separately) and 'Income tax expense' (which is mapped separately). This follows standard practice for an integrated oil & gas company, where cost of goods sold (crude purchases), production, SG&A, depreciation, exploration, pension, and other operating taxes are all operating costs. 3. 'Other taxes and duties' is included in total_operating_cost as it is described as an operating cost in the supplementary notes (Note 19) and is part of the 'Costs and other deductions' section. 4. 'Net income' uses the line attributable to the parent company ('Net income (loss) attributable to ExxonMobil'). 5. 'Taxes' is mapped directly from 'Income tax expense (benefit)'. 6. 'Interest expenses' is mapped directly from 'Interest expense'. 7. All values are extracted from the primary statement. The supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns but do not change the top-line values used for extraction. 8. The scale is 'millions of dollars' as stated in the statement header, so scale is 1E6.",
